WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:01.729
What is the next element?

00:00:01.729 --> 00:00:04.330
Hassium, I know nothing about hassium, should
we make

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.839
something up?

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:11.349
Element 108 – Hassium, I know absolutely
nothing about it.

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:16.080
However, the power of the periodic table is
that by looking at

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.820
the periodic table I can say ‘well its chemistry
has got to be a

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:26.599
bit like iron but it won’t be exactly like
iron because iron is a

00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:31.369
light element and as the elements get heavier
going down

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:36.699
that their chemistry changes’. They tend
to have a larger

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:41.040
number of so called oxidation states and so
what I would

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.199
predict was that if hassium was not radioactive
it would still

00:00:44.199 --> 00:00:49.410
be pretty poisonous and it might be an interesting
catalyst it

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:54.070
would probably react with carbon monoxide
and if it was

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.120
stable it would have probably made a great
addition to my

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.469
doctoral thesis work.

